functions:
Functions
  function add(a, b) { return a + b }
  function greet(name='world') { ... }
  let inc = function(x) { return x + 1 }
  function f(...) { ... }            defaults must follow required args
  return expr               return a value

control_flow:
Control flow
  if cond { ... } else if cond { ... } else { ... }
  while cond { ... }
  for x in collection { ... }   iterates lists/strings/dicts/iterators
  for [k, v] in pairs { ... }   destructuring patterns
  break / continue

types:
Types (optional static layer)
  let x: Int = 5
  let y: String? = null
  let r: Result = ...
  type Point = {x: Int, y: Int}
  type Result = Ok value | Err message
  protocol Printable { function to_string() -> String }
  protocol Named = { function name() -> String }
  trait MyTrait   (marker interface)
  function first<T>(items: List<T>) -> T? { ... }
  function show<T: Printable>(value: T) -> String { ... }
  generic calls infer type arguments; bounds are checked statically
  structural conformance reports P201-P205 for protocol method signatures
  conformance is scoped to protocols/traits used as generic bounds
  erase_types strips annotations, generic headers, protocols, and traits before runtime
